hy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and check why an RC that was unhealthy in staging got promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15184, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014zve9Rmippq6tegbQy9sRU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15184, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014zve9Rmippq6tegbQy9sRU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18716, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now healthy. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions are running it, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the result after it. It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018M3krWLV4jHWZaPuUMhWgb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UfL1xwgVJNH83f5mdZ26tt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FJhPdvvXvaSS58xuzCnbqM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QYgNmDBUBsLaowB5p2tJRQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T8P1dao86ytZpCZsJtYkRE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014zve9Rmippq6tegbQy9sRU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and check why an RC that was unhealthy in staging got promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's now healthy. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions are running it, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the result after it. It lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}